From e73cd0e72462ef4fda4dee44d9281443ce438f51 Mon Sep 17 00:00:00 2001
From: Ian Blenke <ian@blenke.com>
Date: Fri, 19 Jun 2026 08:37:56 -0400
Subject: [PATCH 02784/11362] [outer-loop] #3 Free a 3090 for the ARC
 generator: guarded opt-in CUDA toggle

Operator-approved 2026-06-19 (the 3090s have sat idle since the TRM retirement, while LLM induction
on the iGPU is ~4 tok/s). Adds an OPT-IN CARNOT_ARC_GENERATOR_CUDA_GPU=<idx> toggle to
LocalGGUFProposer: when set, the generator runs the local CUDA llama-server pinned to that 3090 via
CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES -- but ONLY if the card has >=13GB free (the yield guard: it falls back to the
iGPU rather than fight a conductor training job for the card). Default (no env) is UNCHANGED (iGPU
HIP build). Server+env are resolved at LAUNCH time so the guard sees live GPU state. Validated:
default->iGPU/env-None; toggle gpu0(free)->CUDA+CUDA_VISIBLE_DEVICES=0; bad/busy idx->guard falls back
to iGPU. 605 tests pass; the 1 ka59 + 3 import failures are pre-existing (reference 0 of the touched
symbols), not from this change.

Co-Authored-By: Claude Opus 4.8 <noreply@anthropic.com>
